        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: थोपना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "थोपना — thopnā — \"to impose, to force (on someone)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कोई तुम पर अपनी राय नहीं थोप सकता। koī tum par apnī rāy nahīṃ thop saktā. Nobody can force their opinion on you."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने अपनी राय थोपी, usne apnī rāy thopī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "थोपना (thopnā) is inherited from stōpyate, \"is obstructed\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 13723). CDIAL glosses the Hindi verb \"to cover, to heap\"; the sense of forcing a thing on someone is not among its glosses, and may have grown from heaping a thing on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
